SignalBoost — Project Documentation
> **Read this first.** This single file explains the entire SignalBoost project: what it is, how it's built, where every file lives, how the pieces connect, and how to do common tasks. A new developer should be able to read this and understand the whole system.
Live site: https://signalboostapp.com
Repo: github.com/SignalBoost/signalboost- (branch: `main`)
Hosting: Vercel (auto-deploys on every commit to `main`)
Last documented: 2026-05-24
---
1. What SignalBoost Is
SignalBoost is a geo-aware affiliate marketplace — positioned as "Your AI-guided digital shopping mall." A visitor lands on the homepage, tells an AI concierge what they need (e.g. "flights to Lima next month"), and gets matched to trusted affiliate partners that serve their region. When they click a partner, they go to that partner's site via an affiliate link; if they buy, SignalBoost earns a commission.
Revenue model: affiliate commissions (Awin, Admitad, Travelpayouts, Amazon).
Audience: human travelers/shoppers, worldwide, 7 languages.
Key differentiator: region-awareness — partners shown actually operate in the visitor's country.
132 partners across 14 categories: flights, hotels, car_rentals, esim, tours, transfers, insurance, travel_services, marketplace, products_tools, finance, specialty_other, health_fitness, sports_outdoors.
7 languages: en, pt-BR, es, pl, de, fr, it.
There is a sibling SaaS product at `saas.signalboostapp.com` (podcast/brand tools) — a separate concern that shares the same Supabase database. Don't confuse the two. Tables prefixed for affiliate use (`affiliate_partners`, `partner_clicks`, `partner_searches`) belong to THIS marketing site; tables like `partners` (podcasts), `profiles`, `subscriptions` belong to the SaaS side.
