5. Data & Database (Supabase)
Supabase project ref: `dwchaygtxubufxkzfpne` (shared with the SaaS side).
Tables owned by THIS site
Table	Purpose	Key columns
`affiliate_partners`	The 132 partners (the directory)	id, name, category, category_key, category_label, network, logo, description, tier, featured, travel_related, regions (JSON text), url, regional_urls (JSON text), placements (JSON text)
`partner_clicks`	Logged partner clicks (anonymous)	id, partner_id, partner_name, query, region
`partner_searches`	Logged searches (anonymous)	id, query, intent, region, results_count, no_results
RLS (Row Level Security) is DISABLED on these three (they're public-readable directory + anonymous logging). `affiliate_partners` has UNIQUE constraints on both `id` and `url` (two-lock duplicate prevention).
Nested fields (`regions`, `regional_urls`, `placements`) are stored as JSON text (because CSV import is flat) and parsed back in code.
IMPORTANT — partner `url` is an AFFILIATE REDIRECT (awin1.com, *.tpo.lv, admitad redirect domains), NOT the partner's real website. This matters for logos: you cannot derive a brand domain from `url`. The marquee uses a hardcoded id→domain map instead (see §16). If a real `domain` column is ever added to `affiliate_partners`, the marquee can be simplified to read it directly.
Static fallback
`public/partners.json` — the 132 partners as a static file. If Supabase is empty/unreachable, the site falls back to this so partners never disappear. Keep it roughly in sync with the DB as a safety net.
How partners are loaded
`lib/home/partners-source.ts` → `loadPartners()` reads `affiliate_partners`, decodes JSON fields, falls back to `public/partners.json` on empty/error.
`app/api/partners/route.ts` → GET endpoint that returns `loadPartners()` (60s cache).
`HomeApp.tsx` fetches `/api/partners` (then falls back to `/partners.json` directly). Triple safety net.
