16. Partner Logo Marquee (logo.dev)  [ADDED 2026-05-24]
What it is: a two-row scrolling "Window Shopping" marquee near the top of the homepage showing real brand logos of FEATURED partners. Borrowed-trust element.
Files:
  - `components/PartnerMarquee.tsx` — the component. Receives `partnersData` and `lang` props from HomeApp.
  - `components/marquee.css` — scoped styles (dark glass cards; scroll animation duration 70s = slower; hover pauses).
How it picks brands: filters `partnersData` to `featured === true` AND present in the `BRAND_DOMAINS` map (id → real brand domain) at the top of PartnerMarquee.tsx. This means it ONLY shows curated, recognizable featured brands — never the full 132, and never a brand without a known real domain.
Why a domain map (important): partner `url` is an affiliate redirect, so a logo can't be derived from it (that produced wrong/generic logos). The map supplies each featured brand's REAL website (e.g. trivago → trivago.com) so logo.dev returns the correct logo. Links still use the affiliate `url` (revenue-safe).
Logo source: logo.dev. URL form `https://img.logo.dev/<domain>?token=<NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGO_DEV_TOKEN>&size=128&format=png&retina=true`. Token is a publishable key in Vercel env (§11). Each logo sits on a small white chip so dark brand marks stay visible on the dark cards. `onError` hides a failed logo → clean name-only card. (Clearbit was the original plan/roadmap but its free API was shut down 2026-12-08; logo.dev replaced it.)
Heading text: "WINDOW SHOPPING" + subtitle, localized via i18n keys `window_shopping` / `marquee_subtitle` (all 7 languages).
Wiring: HomeApp renders `<PartnerMarquee lang={lang} partnersData={...} />` on the concierge landing view, inside a wrapper div, only when partners have loaded.
To maintain: add/remove brands by editing the BRAND_DOMAINS map; fix a wrong logo by correcting that brand's domain there.
