17. Support Email Infrastructure (ImprovMX)  [ADDED 2026-05-24]
Goal: professional support addresses at the domain that forward to the owner's personal Gmail, while being able to tell which platform an inquiry is about.
Provider chain: Namecheap (domain registrar + DNS) → ImprovMX (free email forwarding) → Gmail (cadomos@gmail.com, the destination inbox).
Why ImprovMX: the domain's DNS is on Namecheap (NOT Vercel — Vercel only hosts the site). Vercel doesn't do email. ImprovMX forwards with no nameserver change.
DNS records (in Namecheap → Advanced DNS):
  - Mail Settings switched from "Email Forwarding" to "Custom MX".
  - MX `@` → `mx1.improvmx.com` (priority 10)
  - MX `@` → `mx2.improvmx.com` (priority 20)
  - TXT `@` (SPF) → `v=spf1 include:spf.efwd.registrar-servers.com include:spf.improvmx.com ~all`  (keeps Namecheap's SPF + adds ImprovMX; ONE combined SPF record only)
  - Untouched/kept: A `@`→76.76.21.21 (Vercel site), CNAME `saas`→cname.vercel-dns.com, CNAME `www`→cname.vercel-dns.com, TXT `@` admitad-verification.
Aliases (in ImprovMX dashboard, all forward to cadomos@gmail.com):
  - `support@signalboostapp.com`   → SignalBoost (this affiliate site)
  - `service@signalboostapp.com`   → SaaS platform  (NOTE: owner considered renaming to `saassupport@` for clarity — confirm final name; whatever is live should be reflected on each platform's contact page)
  - `*` (catch-all) also exists → forwards everything to the Gmail.
How to tell platforms apart: each platform displays a DIFFERENT alias, so the email's "To:" line identifies the source platform. (Optional: Gmail filters can auto-label/color by destination address.)
Status: INBOUND forwarding is live and tested (emails to the aliases arrive in Gmail). OUTBOUND "send as" (replies showing the support address) is NOT yet set up — see Roadmap §15 item 1.
To manage: aliases in ImprovMX (app.improvmx.com); DNS in Namecheap (Advanced DNS); outbound in Gmail Settings → Accounts.
